# ---------------- Marine.events (Task 27 Part F example) ----------------
# Ranged infantry with a stim-pack ability, written against the words Tasks 27 C/E added.
#
# WHAT IT SHOWS
#   · the stim cost is spent from the unit's own `my Mana`
#   · the speed boost is a buff ("stim", 8 s, +40 Speed, refreshing rather than stacking)
#   · the ability's lockout is one shared timer: `my "stim" is ready` gates it and
#     `my "stim" cooldown` is the seconds left, so no `when every 1 seconds` poll is needed
#   · `bind` drives a command-card label from that cooldown with no extra event
#
# SETUP (editor): an EventSheet on the unit whose Event File is `Marine`. The selection
# ring and control groups are automatic (Task 18 Part A) — the scene owns the ring actors.
# Task 19 Part A grows this into the full unit: attack, weapon data and the typed stats stay
# in the unit table, not here.
#
# The label and bar are optional: they resolve by actor name, so a scene without them simply
# shows nothing. Rename them here if your command card uses other names.
bind StimLabel to my "stim" cooldown

when me appears
  set my unit type to "land"
  set my attack type to "ranged"
  set my attack range to 300
  set my MaxHealth to 45
  set my Health to 45
  set my Speed to 90
  set my Mana to 100
  set my StimCost to 25

# ---- stim pack (Q) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both conditions gate every line below them, so a cooling or tired marine spends nothing.
when Q is pressed
  my "stim" is ready
  my Mana is higher than my StimCost
  deduct my StimCost from my Mana
  add buff "stim" to me for 8 seconds adding 40 to my Speed
  put "stim" on cooldown for 10 seconds
  play sound "stim"

# The buff puts the speed back on its own when it ends; the cooldown ends on its own too.
# A second press during either one is refused above, not queued.

when my Health becomes 0
  destroy me
